      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "VAN HOVEN (5) shouldered the 59kg from the awkward gate with a tenacious on-speed second over 1600m at Kembla Grange in a stronger race. Will handle the extra trip and take catching with the key jockey change. MY CARTOUCHE (6) handled the rise in trip and grade when she boxed on late to finish a narrow second over this distance at Randwick Kensington. Will roll forward again and give plenty cheek. LORD WOOTTON (8) well bred gelding who struck trouble at the start on debut with a plugging sixth over 1400m at Newcastle. Anticipating sharp improvement over the extra journey. WHAT SHE'S HAVING (7) has been thereabouts in recent runs and the visors go on today. Only fair last start with a plugging fifth in a C1 at Newcastle over 1850m. Minor place chance.",
